## WR-04 — STILL LIVE (judgment call: validator IS attached → drop the parse)

`grep -rn "setValidatorCompiler" apps/api/src` →
`apps/api/src/plugins/zod-type-provider.ts:21  app.setValidatorCompiler(validatorCompiler)`.
The `zodTypeProvider` fastify-plugin is registered at the buildApp boundary
(`index.ts:169` import; registered before routes). `agent/stream.ts` declares
`schema: { body: AgentStreamRequestSchema }` at :122. With the validator
compiler attached, Fastify runs declarative `schema.body` validation BEFORE
the handler — ALWAYS, regardless of `reply.hijack()` (hijack happens inside the
handler, long after validation). The `:118-121` comment claiming the manual
parse is needed "because zod-type-provider's auto-400 path runs AFTER Fastify's
body parser" is misleading: schema validation runs before the handler and a
ZodError is routed through `registerErrorHandler` already.

DETERMINATION: validator IS attached → the inline `AgentStreamRequestSchema.parse`
at :159 is genuinely redundant. WR-04 fix = DROP the parse, use the
type-provider-typed `req.body`, correct the comment. (This differs from Phase 64
H-1's conversations routes, which KEPT the inline parse because those routes
deliberately do NOT declare `schema.body` — confirmed `streaming-usage.ts:64-67`
and `web-search.ts:93` both comment "we do NOT register schema.body". The
agent/stream route DOES declare it, so the parse is dead defence here.)
DISPOSITION: STILL LIVE — drop the parse per Task 4.

