## WR-09 — STILL LIVE (judgment call: Option A — document sentinel + assert relative)

`grep -n "http://internal" apps/api/src/routes/realtime.ts`
→ :189 — `new URL(rawUrl, "http://internal")` then `req.raw.url` in-place mutation
inside the `preHandler`.

DECISION: Option A (document + assert relative). Rationale:
- Option B (proxy URL-rewrite hook) is NOT cleanly available: `@fastify/http-proxy@11.4.4`
  exposes `wsClientOptions.rewriteRequestHeaders` (headers only — already used at
  realtime.ts:152) but NO per-request upstream-URL rewrite hook. The plugin reads
  `req.raw.url` directly when wiring the WSS upgrade — there is no documented
  `preRewrite`/`rewriteRequestUrl` seam in 11.4.4. Forcing a rewrite would be a
  fragile reach into plugin internals (CLAUDE.md hard rule 1 — no fragile invention).
- Option A is the genuine improvement: the `"http://internal"` sentinel is a
  documented WHATWG-URL parser base (host never used); a guard that throws if
  `rawUrl` is ever absolute makes the silent scheme/host-drop bug surface loudly.
  The in-place mutation stays (the plugin requires it) but is the LAST statement
  in the `preHandler` with a comment that the user id deliberately enters
  `req.raw.url` only immediately before the upgrade.
DISPOSITION: STILL LIVE — Option A per Task 5.

